<Legal title="Privacy notice" description="What personal data the hosted FlutterProbe services and this website handle, why, for how long, and how to exercise your rights." other="/aviso-de-privacidad/">
  <p>This is a translation for your convenience. The <a href="/aviso-de-privacidad/" hreflang="es">Spanish version</a> (aviso de privacidad integral) is the binding one, and it prevails if the two differ.</p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible for your data</h2>
  <p>The party responsible for the personal data described here is:</p>
  <LegalEntity />
  <p>("we"). This notice covers this website and the hosted FlutterProbe services (Probe Cloud and its dashboard). The command line tool, the Dart agent and Probe Studio run on your machine and send us nothing unless you upload to a hosted service.</p>

  <h2>2. The data we handle</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Account and sign-in:</strong> the email address you sign in with, the team you belong to, and the records of your sign-ins and sessions.</li>
    <li><strong>Billing:</strong> the billing email address, the customer, subscription and invoice records that our payment provider keeps for us, and the tax details you send us if you ask for a tax invoice. We do not receive or store full card numbers.</li>
    <li><strong>Run reports you upload:</strong> the test results and, with them, what your tests and configuration put into the report: test and file names, error messages (shortened, and with paths and secret-looking values removed by the command line tool before the upload), the device name, the operating system version, the application identifier and version, the configuration file name, tags, performance figures, the properties you set, the agent version and the locale. Screenshots, videos, logs and device identifiers are not uploaded.</li>
    <li><strong>Details of the build that uploaded:</strong> the repository, branch, commit, pull request and run number, and the identity token that your build system issues for the upload, which we check and do not keep.</li>
    <li><strong>Security records:</strong> a shortened one-way hash of the IP address of a request, used to count requests and stop abuse; the IP address itself is held in memory for about one minute by the payment service and is not stored. We keep a record of security-relevant actions (such as sign-ins, uploads and changes to a team) with hashed identifiers; some of those records contain the repository name and the team identifier.</li>
    <li><strong>Messages:</strong> what you write to us by email, and the record of the emails we send you (address, content, and whether the message was delivered).</li>
    <li><strong>This website:</strong> it sets no cookies and has no analytics. The company that hosts it receives the IP address and the browser details of each request, as any web host does.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do not ask for sensitive personal data, and the services are not meant for it. Do not put it into your tests or reports.</p>

  <h2>3. What we use it for</h2>
  <p>We use the data only for these purposes, all of which are necessary to provide the services you ask for:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>to create your account, sign you in and show your team its results;</li>
    <li>to store and process the reports you upload, and to compute the summaries the dashboard shows;</li>
    <li>to charge for paid plans, send invoices and the notices about renewals, and keep the accounting records the law requires;</li>
    <li>to keep the services secure, prevent abuse and investigate incidents;</li>
    <li>to answer your messages and send you notices about the service and about changes to its terms;</li>
    <li>to comply with the law and with orders of competent authorities.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We have no secondary purposes. We do not use your data for advertising, we do not sell it, we do not build profiles of you, and we make no decisions about you by automated means alone. We do not send marketing email.</p>
  <p>Where the law requires your consent, you give it when you create an account or send us data after this notice has been made available to you. You can revoke it as section 7 describes.</p>

  <h2>4. Who receives it</h2>
  <p>We use service providers that process data on our behalf and on our instructions (encargados): for payments, hosting and storage, email delivery and the hosting of this website. They are named, with what each receives, on the <a href="/subprocessors/">subprocessors page</a>. Some of them operate outside Mexico, including in the United States of America. Passing data to them is not a transfer to a third party under Mexican law.</p>
  <p>We do not transfer your personal data to third parties for their own purposes. We disclose it without your consent only in the cases the law provides, for example when a competent authority orders it with legal grounds. If any other transfer were ever needed, we would ask for your consent first.</p>

  <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Runs and daily summaries:</strong> deleted at the latest 365 days after the upload.</li>
    <li><strong>Details of results that did not pass:</strong> deleted by whole calendar month, once that month ended more than 90 days ago (so at the latest about four months after the upload).</li>
    <li><strong>Account and team data:</strong> while the account exists, and deleted on request (section 7).</li>
    <li><strong>Billing and accounting records:</strong> for the period that tax and commercial law require.</li>
    <li><strong>Security records:</strong> while the services operate, because they are needed to detect and prove misuse.</li>
    <li><strong>Emails with us:</strong> while they are needed to deal with your request and to document it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>The dashboard has no button to delete your own data yet. Write to us and we delete it by hand, except what the law requires us to keep.</p>

  <h2>6. Cookies</h2>
  <p>This website sets no cookies and uses no web beacons or similar tracking technology. The dashboard of the hosted services sets two cookies, both strictly necessary to sign in, readable only by our server and sent only over an encrypted connection:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>probe_login</code>, for 15 minutes, to complete a sign-in;</li>
    <li><code>probe_session</code>, for the session length you choose when you sign in (1 to 30 days), holding the team and session identifiers.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>You can block or delete them in your browser; without them you cannot sign in. They are not used to follow you across sites, and no data from them is passed to anyone else.</p>

  <h2>7. Your rights (ARCO) and how to use them</h2>
  <p>You have the right to access your personal data, to have it rectified when it is inaccurate or incomplete, to have it cancelled (deleted) and to oppose its use. You may also revoke the consent you gave, and ask us to limit the use or disclosure of your data.</p>
  <p>To do any of these, send an email to <a href="mailto:support@alphawavesystems.com">support@alphawavesystems.com</a> with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>your name and the email address where you want the answer;</li>
    <li>a document that shows who you are or, if you act for someone else, that you represent them;</li>
    <li>a clear description of the data and of the right you want to exercise;</li>
    <li>anything that helps us find the data, such as the email address of the account or the name of the team; for a rectification, the correct data and a document that supports it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If something is missing we ask you for it. We answer within 20 business days of receiving a complete request, and if the request is granted we carry it out within the following 15 business days. The law allows each of these periods to be extended once, for the same length, when the case justifies it. The procedure is free. We answer by email, and access is given as an electronic copy.</p>
  <p>Revoking consent or cancelling data that we need in order to provide the services means that we close the account. Some data cannot be deleted at once because the law requires us to keep it; in that case we block it and use it only for that purpose.</p>
  <p>Because we do not use your data for advertising, there is no exclusion list to join. To limit a use or disclosure, write to the same address.</p>
  <p>If you believe your right to the protection of your personal data has been infringed, or you do not agree with our answer, you may go to the Secretaría Anticorrupción y Buen Gobierno, the Mexican authority for personal data protection, within the period the law sets (15 business days from our answer, or from the end of the period we had to answer).</p>

  <h2>8. Security</h2>
  <p>We apply administrative, technical and physical measures to protect personal data against loss, alteration, destruction and unauthorised use or access: among others, encrypted connections, access limited to what each function needs, secrets kept apart from the application's data, and records of security-relevant actions. No system is perfectly secure. If a security breach significantly affects your rights, we tell you without delay so that you can protect yourself.</p>

  <h2>9. When we act for our customers</h2>
  <p>The reports a team uploads may contain personal data that the team's organisation decides to put there. For that data the organisation is the party responsible, and we process it only on its behalf, to provide the services. If you are a person named in such a report, address your request to that organisation; if you write to us, we pass the request on to it. Organisations that need a data processing agreement can ask us for one.</p>

  <h2>10. If you are in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom</h2>
  <p>Where the data protection law of your country applies to us, this section applies too.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Legal bases:</strong> we process account, report and billing data to perform the contract with you or your organisation; security records because of our legitimate interest in keeping the services secure and preventing abuse; and accounting records to comply with legal obligations.</li>
    <li><strong>Your rights:</strong> access, rectification, erasure, restriction, portability and objection, in the cases the law provides, and the right to withdraw consent where processing is based on it. Use the procedure in section 7.</li>
    <li><strong>Complaints:</strong> you may complain to the data protection authority of your country.</li>
    <li><strong>Other countries:</strong> your data is processed in Mexico and in the countries where our providers operate, including the United States of America. These countries may not protect personal data in the same way as yours. We have not verified in which region each provider stores data, and we do not promise that your data stays in one region.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>11. Minors</h2>
  <p>The services are for professionals. They are not directed to anyone under 18, and we do not knowingly collect their data. If you believe a minor has given us data, write to us and we delete it.</p>

  <h2>12. Changes to this notice</h2>
  <p>We may change this notice when the law, the services or our providers change. The current version, with its number and date, is always on this page. When a change affects how we use your data, we also tell account holders by email before it applies.</p>
</Legal>
